    "content": "All 22 checklist items have been tested and recorded.\n\n## Summary\n\nI tested the CuratedPicks product recommendation site against all 22 checklist items. **18 PASSED, 4 FAILED.**\n\n**Failures found:**\n\n1. **FT-2** – The homepage \"View all\" link under Featured products goes to `/products?featured=true`, but the products page ignores that query parameter and shows all products, not just featured ones. There's no other way to browse the complete set of featured products beyond the homepage's fixed 3-item preview.\n\n2. **FT-4** – Newly assigned tags (via create or edit) never appear as selectable options in the products page's tag filter list, even though they correctly show on the product and work in keyword search.\n\n3. **FT-19** – The admin panel has no backend persistence: newly created products and edits to existing products vanish after a page reload, reverting to the original 9 seed products.\n\n4. **CS-20** – A product can be published with only a name and short description — missing image, retailer link, full review, and specifications are not enforced, and such incomplete products immediately go live on the public site.\n\n**Notable passes worth highlighting:** CRUD changes do reflect immediately within the same browser session across all views (FT-1, FT-6, FT-7); search, sort, category, price-range, rating, and multi-tag OR-filtering all work correctly and update live (FT-3, FT-8–10, IX-13/21, CS-11/12); navigation, purchase links, and not-found states behave correctly (IX-14/15, CS-22); and content stays consistent across homepage/category/list/detail views (CT-16–18)."
  }
}
